"""Single-file BGK acoustics with kinetic momentum reconstruction.

Of the nine architectures in ARCHS (see the "architectures.py" section
below), SIREN, SineKAN, and HWF-KAN are the three models this manuscript
proposes/highlights; tanh-MLP (PINN), Chebyshev-KAN, B-spline-KAN,
Wavelet-KAN, Wavelet-PINN, and HWF-PINN are the baselines they are
compared against in the forward (Sec. 4.3, 9-architecture) and inverse
(Sec. 5, 7-architecture) comparison tables.

Install: python -m pip install numpy scipy matplotlib jax optax
Quick checks: python boltzmann_bgk_kinetic.py self_test
Short training: python boltzmann_bgk_kinetic.py kinetic_reconstruction --epochs 100
Full demo: python boltzmann_bgk_kinetic.py kinetic_reconstruction --epochs 3000 --kn-estimate 0.012
--kn is used only to GENERATE synthetic measurements; --kn-estimate is an
optional independently obtained estimate used in reconstruction. Without it,
tau is jointly fitted (exploratory; identifiability is not guaranteed).

Sensor API: reconstruct_kinetic_sensors(t,x_sensor,p_meas,u_meas,...).
The new distribution network uses positive g,h, hard known initial data,
BGK closure, and kinetic momentum flux integral(v**2*g dv). No reference
stress is used in its loss. All previously published metrics need rerunning:
the reference solver now computes equilibrium AFTER streaming and conserves
discrete collision moments; snapshot timestamps are also corrected.
Legacy forward/inverse experiments are retained, not revalidated benchmarks.
The legacy continuum threshold remains 1e-2; the supplied manuscript used
1e-3. Set/report a consistent convention before recomputing classifications.
"""
import os, sys, json, time
import numpy as np
import jax
jax.config.update("jax_enable_x64", True)
import jax.numpy as jnp
from jax import random
import optax
from scipy.optimize import curve_fit
